※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4437

※ A condition asks a question, and a question is answered by a truth value.  A
※ number is not one: C treats any scalar as a condition, which is why `while
※ (n)` counts down in C and means nothing here.  Where the question is whether
※ a number has reached zero, `n ≠ 0u8` asks it.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: mut u8 = 3u8
    while n:
        n ← n - 1u8
    n
